# Every text file of the plugin is checked out with LF line endings on every platform.
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which would otherwise give the hook and
# helper scripts CRLF endings (bash then fails on `$'\r'`) and the skills, routes and
# allowlist CRLF endings the parsers do not expect. Claude Code installs plugins with Git,
# so this also applies to every employee's installed copy.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Run under bash on every platform, including Windows Git Bash.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

*.gif binary
